{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "303",
   "text": "Why is Europe losing ground to China in trade, and what should it do about it?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "304",
   "text": "China's trade war tools are industrial policy and a weak currency, not tariffs",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "305",
   "text": "Chinese firms, private or state-linked, accept low returns on equity and build too much",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "306",
   "text": "A trading partner's surplus drains demand from your economy; manufacturing capacity has strategic value beyond its profits",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "hidden_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "307",
   "text": "European exports to China down about 0.5 percentage points of European GDP; EU trade deficit with China set to double between 2020 and 2025; European auto exports to China on track for about $10 billion by 2027; Chinese electric vehicle exports at a 3 million annual pace in the second quarter; net exports added about 2 percentage points to Chinese growth over four quarters; yuan weaker against the euro",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#E1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "308",
   "text": "Centre for European Reform brief on German industry; Financial Times, New York Times and Wall Street Journal sector reporting; Adam Tooze; German customs data",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_source",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#E2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "309",
   "text": "Competing local governments add subsidized capacity, which drives profits down and pushes output China cannot absorb into exports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "310",
   "text": "State banks keep the yuan weak; its fall against the euro has roughly offset the EU's 17 percent countervailing duty on BYD",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "311",
   "text": "The second China shock is eroding Europe's core export sectors and is large enough to matter for the whole economy, especially Germany's stagnation",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "312",
   "text": "China is winning a trade war with Europe; Europe needs a counter-industrial policy, broader tariffs on Chinese autos and new pressure for the yuan to rise",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "313",
   "text": "Europe's inadequate response so far; Trump-style tariffs or commodity purchase deals as the fix",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "314",
   "text": "The United States is still importing, which limits the damage, but American firms will not absorb tariff costs much longer",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "315",
   "text": "China's long-standing tariff walls (25 percent on autos) also helped build the sector",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "other_explanation",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_2025-07-28_china-eu-trade-war#R1"
  },
